{
  "tema": 7037,
  "slug": "quedar-quedarse-quedarle",
  "titulo": "Quedar, quedarse and quedarle: the different meanings of quedar",
  "subtitulo": "Quedan dos tacos, quedé con Beto, me quedo aquí, te queda bien.",
  "foto": "t02.jpg",
  "regla": "Quedar = to be left / to arrange to meet (quedar con) / to end up (+ adjective). Quedarse = to stay / to keep (quedarse con). Quedarle = to fit, to suit / to have left (me quedan 20 pesos).",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Quedar** is a very flexible verb. Its meaning changes with how you use it:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Form",
            "Meaning",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "quedar (3rd person)",
              "_to be left, remain_",
              "Quedan dos plátanos."
            ],
            [
              "quedar (con alguien)",
              "_to arrange to meet, to meet_",
              "Quedé con Beto a las ocho."
            ],
            [
              "quedar + adjective",
              "_to end up, be left_ (the result)",
              "Quedó satisfecha."
            ],
            [
              "quedarse",
              "_to stay_",
              "Me quedo en casa."
            ],
            [
              "quedarse con",
              "_to keep_",
              "Me quedo con la azul."
            ],
            [
              "quedarse + adjective",
              "_to become, be left_ (a change)",
              "Se quedó dormido."
            ],
            [
              "quedarle (me, te, le…)",
              "_to fit, to suit_",
              "Esa camisa te queda bien."
            ],
            [
              "quedarle (me, te, le…)",
              "_to have left_",
              "Me quedan veinte pesos."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To arrange to meet, Mexico more often says **quedar de** + infinitive: **quedé de verme con Beto a las ocho**, **¿quedamos de vernos?**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Quedar** for _to be left_ only uses the 3rd person: **queda / quedan**, **quedó / quedaron**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Quedarle** works like **gustar**: the thing is the subject, the person goes in the pronoun."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: with no pronoun, things remain; with **se**, people stay; with **le**, it's about you."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
